EXT. SPARKLE AUTO SPA CAR WASH - NIGHT

Neon pink. A conveyor belt rumbles through a tunnel of foaming brushes. A dented sedan idles at the entrance, hazards blinking.

VINNIE CASTELLANOS, 40s, leather jacket, keys in one fist, slams the sedan's trunk. LUCKY SZYMANSKI, 30s, kneels by the front tire, holding a duffel bag. A police radio on Vinnie's belt crackles.

SGT. HAYES (V.O.)
(over radio)
All units, shots fired at Third and Maple. Suspects in a gray sedan.

VINNIE
(muttering)
Too soon.

LUCKY
We gotta go, Vin.

VINNIE
Wait for Dee.

LUCKY
Dee's three minutes late.

VINNIE
She's two minutes late. Don't--

DEE OKPARA, 30s, black hoodie, running shoes, bursts around the corner of the tunnel with a gym bag clutched to her chest.

DEE
Go, go, go!

LUCKY
You're late!

DEE
I was shot at!

VINNIE
By who?

DEE
By whoever I robbed, Vinnie, who do you think?

SGT. HAYES (V.O.)
(over radio)
Units responding to Third and Maple. Repeat, gray sedan, plates unknown.

Vinnie rips the radio off his belt and drops it into the car-wash foam. Dee dives into the back seat. Lucky tosses the duffel in after her and slides behind the wheel.

LUCKY
Vin, door!

VINNIE
I'm getting in!

The sedan lurches forward onto the belt. Brushes descend. Water sprays across the windshield. Inside, three people sit very still, breathing hard, as the car wash whirls around them and a siren grows in the distance.

DEE
This is the worst getaway ever.

LUCKY
It's a very good wash.
